from pathlib import Path
import json
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;D=R/'data';out=D/'training-report';out.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
s=json.loads((D/'training-summary/summary.json').read_text());items=json.loads((D/'training-summary/histories.json').read_text())
head=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>All training histories: five-parameter cones</title><style>body{{font:16px system-ui;max-width:1100px;margin:30px auto;padding:0 20px;background:#faf9f6;color:#223}}section{{background:white;border:1px solid #ddd;border-radius:8px;padding:20px;margin:20px 0}}table{{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}}td,th{{text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;padding:9px}}img{{width:100%}}select,input{{font:inherit;max-width:100%}}a{{color:#136d8b}}</style><h1>Five-parameter cones: all rotation-0 training data</h1><p><a href="../index.html">Original 48-history cone/ovoid comparison</a></p><section><h2>Complete extraction</h2><p><b>{s['training_histories']:,} training histories · {s['frames']:,} saved frames · {s['active_frames']:,} active frames</b>. Exact frozen training IDs and timestamps verified. No validation or test histories included. No new simulations or neural training.</p><p>Sources: 1,255 retained local temperature volumes and 407 existing local archives, verified by SHA-256. Read one history at a time; no downloaded or decoded full-field copy retained.</p><p>The five values are pivot height, downwind tilt, axial length, end radius, and maximum gas temperature inside the cone. They describe instantaneous saved fields, approximately 2 s apart ({s['min_saved_step_s']:.3f}–{s['max_saved_step_s']:.3f}s), not the maximum between frames.</p></section><section><h2>Measured fit</h2><table><tr><th>Shape</th><th>Median hot capture</th><th>Median purity</th><th>Median IoU</th></tr>'''
for label,key in [('Cone','cone'),('Original 2σ ovoid','ovoid2sigma'),('Ovoid expanded to 95%','ovoid95')]:
 a=s['active_frame_medians'][key];head+='<tr><td>'+label+'</td>'+''.join(f'<td>{a[k]:.1%}</td>' for k in ['hot_recall','hot_precision','iou'])+'</tr>'
head+=f'''</table><p>Hot means gas above 50°C, not flame or ignition. Capture measures hot cells enclosed; purity measures enclosed cells that are hot. These are active-frame medians; equal-configuration-weighted means are separately recorded in the summary JSON.</p><p>Ground-level apex selected in{s['ground_apex_fraction']:.1%} of active frames. Domain peak missed by the cone in{s['domain_peak_missed_frames']:,} active frames. These are geometric compromises, not proof of physical pivot locations. The ovoid has more geometric freedom than the cone.</p><img src="summary/distributions.png" alt="Five parameter distributions and cone versus ovoid purity"></section><section><h2>Inspect any training history</h2><select id="case"></select><p id="condition"></p><label>Frame <input id="time" type="range" min="0" max="90" value="10"></label><p id="frame"></p><table id="values"></table><p><a id="download">Download this full history</a></p><p id="error"></p></section><section><h2>What this means for a future loss</h2><p>There are 94,183 inactive frames and 57,059 active frames. First predict whether a cone is present; compare its five values only on active frames. Scale metres, degrees and temperature separately, so temperature does not dominate merely because its numbers are larger.</p><p>A normalized Huber penalty is a candidate baseline: small mistakes receive a smooth penalty, while unusually large mistakes do not dominate as strongly as squared error. This has not been selected or tested. Fitted angles change by up to 70° at the 99th percentile between adjacent active snapshots; these jumps can reflect the coarse fitting search. Report spatial hot-cell coverage and over-coverage as well as parameter error, because different cones can describe similar regions. There are 1,545 active frames (2.71%) with fitted axial length below one 0.5 m cell, down to 0.00020 m. These are degenerate cell-centre fits, not physically resolved flame dimensions, and must be flagged when considering training targets. A loss cannot repair a systematically loose geometric representation.</p></section><section><h2>Downloads and interpretation</h2><p><a href="summary/targets.npz">All target arrays (NPZ)</a> · <a href="summary/parameter-schema.json">Array schema</a> · <a href="summary/summary.json">Full fit and parameter diagnostics</a> · <a href="summary/validation.json">Coverage validation</a></p><p>Inactive frames use active=false and NaN parameter targets; never train regression against those NaNs. No loss function or model has been selected by this extraction.</p><p>Fixed apex x=y=8m, axis constrained to downwind +x / vertical z. Apex is ground or one of seven heights within the crown; tilt has 10° increments. Radius calibrated to enclose 95% of hot cell centres. Coarse fitting is not globally optimal; jumps may reflect switching geometry rather than physical motion. Circular cross section and pointed apex are imposed assumptions.</p><p>Generic vegetation crowns 4–10 m tall, 0.5 m cells, 24×16×16 m observed region, artificial 1500°C igniter for 20 s. No trunks, buildings or embers. Crown geometry varies, including legacy examples. Previously examined simulation data, not physical validation. Hot gas includes the imposed source. No incident heat flux, radiation outside the cone, material ignition or between-frame peak is inferred. Domain-truncated shapes do not describe unseen gas.</p></section>'''
script='''<script>const cases=CASES;let current=null,requestId=0;const q=id=>document.getElementById(id);cases.forEach((c,i)=>{let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=i;o.textContent=c.case;q('case').append(o)});function frame(){if(!current)return;const r=current.snapshots[+q('time').value];q('frame').textContent=r.time_s.toFixed(3)+'s · '+(r.active?'hot cone present':'no cells above 50°C');const entries=[['Pivot height (m)',r.cone?.pivot_height_m],['Tilt from vertical (degrees)',r.cone?.tilt_from_vertical_deg],['Length along axis (m)',r.cone?.length_m],['End radius (m)',r.cone?.end_radius_m],['Peak inside cone (°C)',r.cone?.peak_temperature_C],['Hot-cell capture',r.cone_metrics?.hot_recall],['Hot-cell purity',r.cone_metrics?.hot_precision],['Domain peak (°C)',r.domain_peak_temperature_C]];q('values').innerHTML=entries.map(([k,v])=>'<tr><th>'+k+'</th><td>'+(v==null?'—':v.toFixed(4))+'</td></tr>').join('')}async function load(){const id=++requestId,c=cases[+q('case').value];current=null;q('values').innerHTML='';q('error').textContent='Loading…';q('condition').textContent='Training index ' +c.case_index+'; height ' +c.physical_key[0]+'m; wind ' +c.physical_key[3]+'m/s; fold'+c.fold;const path='histories/'+c.case+'.json';q('download').href=path;try{const res=await fetch(path);if(!res.ok)throw Error('HTTP'+res.status);const data=await res.json();if(id!==requestId)return;current=data;q('error').textContent='';frame()}catch(e){if(id===requestId)q('error').textContent=String(e)}}q('case').onchange=load;q('time').oninput=frame;load();</script></html>'''
(out/'index.html').write_text(head+script.replace('CASES',json.dumps([{k:x[k] for k in ['case','case_index','physical_key','fold']} for x in items])))
